  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday) \nIssued at 1042 PM CDT Sat Oct 3 2026\n\nNot much to report in the extended forecast package with the main \ntheme being the continuation of warmer temperatures and drier \nconditions across the region. Synoptically speaking, the H5 upper \nridge over the SWCONUS will remain encompassed over the region \nbefore we begin to see a slight change in the pattern as the ridge \nbegins to break down in response as weak shortwaves pass through the \nmain flow over the PacNW. Despite this, the continuation of upslope \nflow at the lower-levels will help aid in temperatures from becoming \ntoo warm, thanks to the surface high lingering across the area. As a \nresult, expect highs in the 70s and lower 80s through mid-week \nbefore afternoon temperatures increase above seasonal standards in \nthe mid 80s to lower 90s as lee cyclogenesis develops over \nsoutheastern CO. Precipitation is not expected through the extended \nthanks to lack of moisture and forcing for ascent.",
